        <item>
            <title>3.23.3</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:27:35 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>232</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.23.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's New in 3.23.3</h2><ul></ul><p><strong>Improved</strong></p><ul><li>Folder sorting with Auto starts faster: files that already have AI names are grouped by those names without being read again.</li><li>Sorting with your own folder rule reads each file once instead of twice.</li><li>Sorting starts when you close the sorting settings, so picking a rule no longer starts grouping with the one you didn't want.</li><li>While sorting reads your files, the status shows Reading files, then Grouping files while it plans the folders.</li><li>TV episodes get a season and episode number only when the file name, metadata, subtitles, speech or on-screen text gives it, and an episode without one is named by what happens in it.</li></ul><p><strong>Fixed</strong></p><ul><li>Videos from DVD rips (MPEG-2 in MKV), AVI files, more MKV formats and 4:2:2 Motion JPEG are now named by what they show.</li><li>A song playing in a long video, such as a film soundtrack, no longer becomes the video's name.</li></ul>
]]></description>
